-- title:
--   Kernel of the supersingular attachment map is the Gauss centre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K_2$ be the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images, under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the integral-form ratios of $\Gamma_0(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, an $A$-algebra structure on $K_2$ compatible with the tower, a nonzero $j_2 \in K_2$ whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{numerator series})$ of $j$, and a generator $\varpi$ of the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K_2$ characterised by: $f \in W_0$ iff $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$ for some power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ (the Gauss ring). Let $\mathfrak{y}_2$ be an ideal of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A K₂ j₂`, i.e. of the subalgebra of elements of $K_2$ integral over $A[j_2]$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $w$ be a place of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,M$ generated over $k$ by the $q$-expansions `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k M` — that is, a valuation subring of it containing $k$, distinct from the whole field, whose ideals are principal — which lies in [`ModularCurve.ssPlaces p M k`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularNodePlaces.html#L113), the set of places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace p M k`. Finally let $\rho$ be a ring homomorphism from the chart algebra to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,M$ such that $\rho(\varpi) = 0$, $\rho(j_2) =$ `jGeomGen k M` (the class of `jqModC k`), $\rho$ takes values in the valuation subring of $w$, $\rho(b)$ is a nonunit there exactly when $b \in \mathfrak{y}_2$, and $\rho$ is birational in the sense that every $f$ in the function field can be written $f \cdot b = a$ with $a, b$ in the $k$-subalgebra generated by the range of $\rho$ and $b \ne 0$. The conclusion: for every $b$ in the chart algebra, $b \in \ker \rho$ if and only if $b$, viewed in $K_2$, is a nonunit of $W_0$, i.e. lies in the maximal ideal of the Gauss valuation ring.
--
--   This identifies, among the two valuation rings of $K_2$ lying over the uniformiser that govern the two components of the special fibre of the integral model of $X_0(Mp)$, the one cut out by a supersingular attachment map: the kernel of $\rho$ is the centre of the Gauss ring $W_0$, so $\rho$ reads the component on which $j$ reduces to the $q$-expansion $j$ itself rather than its Frobenius twist. It is used in the construction of a homomorphism from the residue field of the Gauss ring realising the identification of the function field of the supersingular component with the level-$M$ modular function field over $k$.
